1.3.m:
You are the purifying strainer of the Vasu, having a hundred streams; you are the purifying strainer of the Vasus, having a thousand streams.
Free from disease, I unite you with offspring, you who multiply through the increase of wealth.
Swelling with sweetness, rich in ghee, living, may we sit near you living!
You are the cauldron of Mātariśvan;
you are the sky;
you are the earth;
all-sustaining by your highest abode.
You are unbent;
do not stumble!
She is all life;
she is all-embracing;
she is all-sustaining.
The drop is offered;
the droplet is offered;
to Agni, to the high firmament, svāhā! to Heaven and Earth!
Unite, O righteous ones, with the wave, most sweet,
cheering for the winning of wealth!
I curdle you as the portion of Indra with soma.
You are not cast down for Viṣṇu.
O Viṣṇu, protect the oblation!
O Waters, keep watch!

1.6.m:
Shaken off is the demon;
shaken off is the enemy.
You are the skin of Aditi;
may the earth recognise you!
You are the mortar, born of the mountain;
may the skin of Aditi recognise you!
Make the earth firm!
You are the mortar, daughter of the mountain;
may the mountain-born recognise you!
Make heaven firm!
You are the prop of heaven.
You are grain;
delight the gods!
Delight the sacrifice!
Delight the lord of the sacrifice!
Delight me, the leader of the sacrifice!
For out-breath [I take] you;
for diffused breath [I take] you;
for in-breath [I take] you;
for a long course, for life [I take] you.
May the divine Savitṛ of golden hands receive you!
With an unblinking eye I look upon you, for the increase of wealth, for good offspring.

1.7.m:
Burnt up is the demon;
burnt up is the enemy.
Drive away, O Agni, the flesh-consuming fire;
banish the consumer of raw flesh!
Convey hither the place of sacrifice to the gods!
You are firm;
make the earth firm!
Give life;
give breath;
gather his kinsmen around this sacrificer!
You are the maintainer;
make the intermediate space firm!
Give sight;
give hearing;
gather his kinsmen around this sacrificer!
You are the supporter;
make heaven firm!
Give vigor;
give strength;
gather his kinsmen around this sacrificer!
You are order;
make the directions firm!
Give wealth;
give prosperity;
gather his kinsmen around this sacrificer!
You are the restrainer;
make the quarters firm!
Give form;
give color;
gather his kinsmen around this sacrificer!
Piled up are you, piled around, the kinsmen of the sacrificer;
of the Bhṛgus […]
The potsherds that the wise arrange at the hot cauldron,
under the rule of Pūṣan, may Indra and Vāyu release them.

1.10.m:
You are the milk of Pṛśni;
from that of yours which is unexhausted and swelling, I pour out what is swelling.
Praying for goodwill, offspring, fortune, and wealth, / obedient to Agni, having girded myself for righteous action—
O Agni, lord of the house, invite me!
O wives of the gods, invite me!
May I sit near you like Aditi with good sons, like Indrāṇī not a widow!
For food [I take] you!
With an unbeguiled eye I gaze upon you for the increase of wealth, for good offspring!
For strength [I take] you!
You are the tongue of Agni, a good fortress for the gods.
For every abode, for every sacrificial formula [I sprinkle you].
You are the Vaiśvānara oblation, with heightened energy, true in might;
might by name are you;
overcome the enemy, overcome those who fight [us]!
You are of thousandfold power; having wiped it, [I make you ready].
You are the clarified butter of the clarified butter, the oblation of the oblation;
you are besprinkled with truth;
with truth I sprinkle you.
You are brilliance;
you are brightness;
you are light.
You are the dear abode of the gods, the unassailable place of sacrifice to the gods.
For the divine beings worthy of sacrifice I take you.
Singed is the demon;
singed is the enemy.
You are unblunted, destroying rivals;
may I not sever life and breath!
Speedy one, I wipe you, the speedy [spoon], for gaining speed;
may I not sever sight and hearing!
Speedy one, I wipe you, the speedy [spoon], for gaining speed;
may I not sever offspring and womb!
Speedy one, [I wipe] you for gaining speed;
may I not sever the cattle-stall of the sacrificer and the increase of wealth!
Speedy one, I wipe you, the speedy [spoon], for gaining speed.

1.11.m:
O divine waters moving in front, lead this sacrifice forward;
promote the lord of the sacrifice!
Indra chose you in the contest with Vṛtra;
you chose Indra in the contest with Vṛtra.
You are sprinkled.
You are the black [antelope], dwelling in the burrow;
acceptable to Agni I sprinkle you.
You are the altar;
acceptable to the sacrificial grass I sprinkle you.
You are the sacrificial grass;
acceptable to the offering spoons I sprinkle you.
You are the portions of the ancestors;
with strengthening food go to the earth!
You are the topknot of Viṣṇu;
soft as wool, spread abroad, comfortable to sit upon for the gods!
You are the Gandharva Viśvāvasu;
[protect] from every danger!
You are the enclosure of the sacrificer, implored with refreshment;
you are the right arm of Indra;
you are the enclosure of the sacrificer, implored with refreshment;
may Mitra and Varuṇa enclose you with firm ordinance, implored with refreshment!
As an invoker of the banquet, O seer, we, radiant, would kindle you, / O Agni, great in the rite!
May Sūrya protect you from the east from any curse / on the highest vault of heaven!
You two are the arms of Savitṛ, the support of the divine races;
you are the seat of the Vasus, of the Rudras, of the Ādityas.
Come, Juhū, turned toward the ghee, heaven by origin;
Aditi with unbroken wings, beloved of the gods, sit in the dear seat with your dear abode!
Come, Upabhṛt, turned toward the ghee, intermediate space by origin;
Aditi with unbroken wings, beloved of the gods, sit in the dear seat with your dear abode!
Come, Dhruvā, turned toward the ghee, earth by origin;
Aditi with unbroken wings, beloved of the gods, sit in the dear seat with your dear abode!
You are the bull of the Śakvarī [verses], Vāyu by origin;
Aditi with unbroken wings, beloved of the gods, sit in the dear seat with your dear abode!
Firm they have sat in the lap of cosmic order, in the world of righteous action;
guard them, O Viṣṇu;
guard the sacrifice;
guard the lord of the sacrifice;
guard me, the leader of the sacrifice!

2.1.m:
You are givers of moisture;
you are givers of life.
Moistening [waters], help me here!
May the waters moisten [my head] for life,
for long life, for splendor!
O plant, protect him!
O axe, do not harm him!
Seeking the gods, I shave these [hairs];
may I attain subsequent well-being.
May the waters of the desert be auspicious to us, may those of the marshy lands be auspicious to us; / may the waters of the ocean be auspicious to us, and may those of the wells be auspicious to us!
May the waters, our mothers, purify us; may those that purify with ghee cleanse me with ghee; / for the goddesses carry away all defilement; I emerge from them bright and purified.
You are the gift of Soma;
you are the body;
protect my body!
You are the milk of the great ones;
the sap of the waters and plants.
You are the bestower of splendor;
bestow splendor upon me!
You are the pupil of Mitra's eye;
through you I place hatred within, enmity within.
You are the bestower of sight;
bestow sight upon me!
May the lord of thought purify you;
may the lord of speech purify you;
may the divine Savitṛ purify you with an unslit sieve, with the rays of the sun!
With your sieve, O lord of the sieve, for whatever I purify [myself],
may I be capable of that!

2.3.m:
You two are the two artistic forms of Ṛg and Sāman;
I lay hold of you two;
protect me until the conclusion!
You are shelter;
give me shelter!
Homage be to you;
do not harm me!
Sharpen this thought, insight, and skill of the one striving, O divine Varuṇa, / whereby we may cross over all misfortunes; may I mount a well-crossing boat.
I have mounted this good boat, unharmed, carrying across, / with a hundred oars, for well-being.
Heaven and Earth providing good protection, blameless, providing good shelter, Aditi who leads well— / may we mount the divine boat with good oars, guiltless, unswerving, for well-being.
You are strength, belonging to the Aṅgirases, soft as wool;
bestow strength in me;
do not harm me!
You are the knot of Soma's garment;
do not harm me!
You are the womb of Indra;
do not harm me!
For plowing with good grain [I take] you;
make the plowing yield good grain!
You are the shelter of Viṣṇu,
the shelter of the sacrificer;
give me shelter!
Homage be to you;
do not harm me!
Protect me from the flashing light of the stars!
O tree providing a good lap, upright, protect me until the conclusion!
Svāhā, the sacrifice from the mind,
svāhā, from heaven,
svāhā, from earth,
svāhā, from the broad atmosphere,
svāhā, from the wind I receive the sacrifice!

2.4.m:
Prepare the vow [food]!
May I be capable of that!
We meditate on the divine, kindly thought for assistance,
granting splendor, all-nourishing, with good crossings, that it may be in our control.
Whatever gods are born of Manu, yoked by Manu, very skillful, whose father is Dakṣa,
may they protect us;
may they help us;
to them svāhā!
O Agni, wake well; we will rejoice well;
guard us heedfully; place us in front for awakening!
You, O Agni, are the vow-protector among gods and among mortals;
you are to be praised at sacrifices.
Pūṣan of acquisitions!
Soma of riches!
Give so much, O Soma;
bring more!
Divine Savitṛ, bestower of wealth from the good,
may the bestower not be deprived of fulfillment;
may I not be deprived of life, of splendor!
O divine waters, O child of the waters, whatever wave of yours is fit for oblation and full of vigor, may I not trample upon that!
Come with power!
With whatever body of yours is worthy of sacrifice, mount with that!
This is your seasonal womb from which, born, you shone;
knowing it, O Agni, mount it; then increase wealth for us!
We have come to this place of divine worship of the earth, where all the gods found pleasure;
crossing over with Ṛg and Sāman, with Yajus verses, may we rejoice in abundance of wealth with food!

2.5.m:
This is your bright body, this your splendor; unite with it;
go to radiance!
You are swift, held by mind, pleasing to Viṣṇu;
at the instigation of you of true instigation, may I attain restraint of body, svāhā!
You are bright;
you are shining;
you are immortal;
you are the oblation for all the gods;
you are thought;
you are mind;
you are prayer;
you are the sacrificial gift;
you are worthy of sacrifice;
you are of the ruling class;
you are Aditi, double-headed;
as such, be well-facing-forward, well-facing-backward to me!
May Mitra bind you at the foot;
may Pūṣan protect [your] paths;
for Indra the overseer!
May your mother approve you, your father, your brother of the same womb;
[your] companion belonging to the same herd!
As such, O goddess, go to the god,
Soma for Indra!
May Rudra turn you back;
with well-being, as a friend of Soma, come back!
You are Vasvī;
you are Rudrā;
you are Aditi;
you are Ādityā;
you are Candrā;
you are Rudrā;
may Bṛhaspati delight you in benevolence;
Rudra with the Vasus has desired [you]!
On the head of the earth I besprinkle you, on the place of divine worship, on the footprint of Iḍā, full of ghee, svāhā!
Here I cut off the neck of the demon!
Here I cut off the neck of whoever, equal to us or unequal, acts as our adversary!
Rest with us;
with us be your riches;
[may] my riches [increase];
yours, yours are riches;
may I not be separated from abundance of wealth!
The divine goddess Urvaśī has looked [upon you];
with good seed, placing seed,
possessing Tvaṣṭṛ, may we attend you!
Do not steal away my life, nor I yours;
may I find a hero in your presence!

2.6.m:
O divine Sūrya, we will buy Soma;
that we proclaim to you;
for all the gods arrange the seasons,
arrange the sacrificial gifts according to the Ṛṣis, according to the deities;
you belong to us;
your cup is the bright one!
Towards that divine Savitṛ within the two halves [of the world], possessing the insight of a sage,
I sing, of true instigation, bestower of jewels, towards [his] beloved thought.
Whose radiant form, his light, shone high at his instigation;
golden-handed, of good insight, he measured out the heaven with [his] fair shape.
For offspring [I buy] you;
may offspring breathe after you;
do you breathe after offspring!
I buy Soma from you, vigorous, milky, full of virility, of great price, resplendent.
I buy your bright [substance] with bright [substance], shining with shining, immortal with immortal,
the power which is of your cow;
with us are your shining [treasures]!
You are the body of ascetic toil, the form of Prajāpati,
thriving with thousandfold nourishment;
you are bought with the supreme beast;
with us is your kin!
Come to us as Mitra, establishing good friends;
enter Indra’s right thigh, willing him who is willing, gentle to him who is gentle!
Svāna, Bhrāj, Aṅghāri, Bambhāri, Hasta, Suhasta, Kṛśānu—
these are your Soma-purchasers;
guard them;
let them not harm you!
Up with life, with good life, up with the sap of plants,
up with the rain of Parjanya, up have I arisen following the immortals!
Traverse the broad atmosphere!
We have reached the path that goes to well-being, free from harm,
by which one avoids all enemies and finds wealth.
You are the skin of Aditi;
sit on the seat of Aditi!
The bull of all knowledge propped up the sky, he measured out the expanse of the earth;
he sat down over all worlds as sovereign ruler: all these are the ordinances of Varuṇa.
He stretched out the atmosphere among the trees, speed in racers, milk in the inviolable [cows],
Varuṇa set insight in hearts, Agni in clans, the sun in the sky, Soma on the rock.
I have mounted the eye of Sūrya, the pupil of Agni’s eye,
when you go with dappled steeds, shining, wise!

2.7.m:
Come, you two reddish oxen, pressing against the yoke, not slaying heroes, tearless, impelled by the sacred word,
prolonging the life of the sacrifice;
go to the houses with well-being!
You are the yoke-pin;
injure him who injures!
Him who injures us, injure him;
and him whom we injure, injure him too!
You belong to Varuṇa;
you are the prop of Varuṇa!
Move forward, O lord of the world, to all dwellings;
may marauders not find you, may highwaymen not find [you];
may malicious wolves not find you!
Becoming a falcon, fly away
to the house of our sacrificer, prepared!
Homage to the eye of Mitra and Varuṇa! Serve that truth for the great god!
Praise the far-seeing, god-born banner, the son of heaven, Sūrya!
You belong to Varuṇa;
may Varuṇa prop you up!
You are the unfastener of Varuṇa’s prop;
released is the noose of Varuṇa!
You are Varuṇa, whose ordinances are steadfast, whose leaf is unbroken;
descend to the offspring!
You are Varuṇa’s seat of truth;
you are the skin of Aditi;
sit on the seat of Aditi!
Varuṇa, whose ordinances are steadfast, has sat down among the homesteads,
of good insight, for universal sovereignty.
You belong to Varuṇa;
for Varuṇa, you!

2.9.m:
At the impulse of divine Savitṛ, with the arms of the Aśvins, with the hands of Pūṣan, I take you;
you are a woman.
Here I cut off the neck of the Rakṣas.
Here I cut off the neck of him who, whether our equal or unequal, acts as our enemy.
You are Taptāyanī;
you are Vittāyanī.
May she protect me in distress;
may she protect [me] in trembling.
O Agni, O Aṅgiras, who are on this earth, come with the name of Āyu!
With that name of yours which is unassailed, unassailable, with that I place you.
O Agni, O Aṅgiras, who are on the second, who are on the third earth, come with the name of Āyu!
With that name of yours which is unassailed, unassailable, with that I place you.
Agni found the name 'Nabhas'.
You are a lioness;
you are a buffalo cow;
spread out for the gods;
be fit for the gods;
purify yourself for the gods;
adorn yourself for the gods!
May great Vibhrāj drink the Soma mead, bestowing unswerving life upon the lord of the sacrifice;
he who, impelled by the wind, protects by himself, fosters the creatures, shines manifold.
May the Vasus with Indra’s shout protect you from the east;
may the Fathers, swift as thought, protect you from the south;
may Pracetas with the Rudras protect you from the west;
may Viśvakarman with the Ādityas protect you from the north;
may Tvaṣṭṛ with the forms protect you from above!
You are a lioness overcoming rivals, svāhā!
You are a lioness winning the increase of wealth, svāhā!
You are a lioness winning good offspring, svāhā!
You are a lioness winning the Ādityas, svāhā!
You are a lioness; bring hither the gods for the sacrificer who serves the gods, svāhā!
For living beings, you!
You are all-lived;
prop the earth!
You dwell unshakably;
prop the atmosphere!
You dwell firmly;
prop the sky!
You are Agni's nest;
you are Agni's rubbish-filling;
the sacrifice has stood firm.
Like Manu we would set you down, like Manu we would kindle [you];
O Agni, like Manu, O Aṅgiras, sacrifice to the gods for him who serves the gods!

2.10.m:
They harness the mind, and they harness the thoughts, the inspired singers of the inspired, great, wise one;
he alone, knowing the ordinances, arranges the priestly duties; great is the praise of divine Savitṛ.
Heard by the gods, make yourselves proclaimed among the gods!
This Viṣṇu strode out; thrice he planted his foot;
it is gathered up in its dust.
Rich in refreshment, rich in milk be, rich in good pasture, bringing glory to mankind;
you propped apart these two world-halves, O Viṣṇu; you supported the earth all around with pegs.
You belong to Viṣṇu;
may Viṣṇu prop you up!
Either from the sky, O Viṣṇu, or from the earth, or from the great, the wide atmosphere, O Viṣṇu,
fill your hands with many treasures, bestow [them] from the right and from the left!
Now indeed I proclaim the heroic deeds of Viṣṇu, who measured out the earthly spaces,
who propped the upper dwelling place, striding out thrice, the wide-striding one.
You are Viṣṇu's back;
you are Viṣṇu's forehead;
you two are Viṣṇu's corners of the mouth;
you are Viṣṇu's seam;
you are Viṣṇu's firm [point];
you belong to Viṣṇu;
for Viṣṇu, you!
For this is Viṣṇu praised for heroic power, like a dread beast, roaming, dwelling in the mountains,
in whose three wide strides all worlds abide.

2.13.m:
You are Vibhū, the conveyer;
you are Vahni, the bearer of oblations;
you are Śvātra, the mindful;
you are Tutha, the all-knowing;
you are Uśij, the sage;
you are Aṅghāri, Bambhāri;
you are Avasyu, the attentive;
you are Śundhyu, the Mārjālīya;
you are the sovereign, Kṛśānu;
you are the one of the assembly, the Āstavya;
you are Nabha, the fast runner;
you are the unpolished, the conveyer of oblations;
you are Ṛtadhāman, the light of heaven;
you are the ocean, all-embracing;
you are Aja Ekapāt;
you are Ahi Budhnya;
you are Kavya, the bearer of the Kavya oblations.
With your terrible troop, protect me, O Agni!
Rescue me, O Agni!
Homage be to you!
Do not harm me!

3.9.m:
Possessed of oblation are these waters; possessed of oblation is the divine sacrifice;
possessed of oblation, he seeks to win [them]; possessed of oblation let Sūrya be!
I seat you in the seat of Agni whose home is not fallen;
desirous of favor, for the benevolent one, establish favor!
You are the portions of Indra and Agni;
you are the portions of Mitra and Varuṇa;
you are the portions of all the gods;
the Vasatīvarī [waters] of Soma!
For the heart, you;
for the mind, you;
for heaven, you;
for Sūrya, you!
Raise this sacrifice aloft to heaven, among the gods; hold fast the priestly services!
O King Soma, descend to all creatures;
may all creatures descend to you!
May Agni hear my call along with the kindling stick; may the waters and the divine vessels hear!
Hear, O pressing stones, now the sacrifice of the wise one; may the god Savitṛ hear my call!
O divine waters, son of the waters, the wave that is fit for oblation, powerful, most intoxicating—that [wave] give you to the gods, among the gods, to the drinkers of pure [Soma], whose portion you are, svāhā!
You are furrow-drawn.
For the non-exhaustion of the ocean, I draw you up.
May Varuṇa, Mitra, Agni unite you; Indra, Bṛhaspati unite [you];
Tvaṣṭṛ, Viṣṇu, rejoicing together with offspring, may he bestow wealth upon the sacrificer!
Yoke-pin by yoke-pin, may they fit according to the yokes!
Whom in battles, O Agni, you protect, the mortal whom in contests you impel,
he obtains perpetual refreshments. Svāhā.
You are the foot-washing [waters] of the Vasus, the Rudras, the Ādityas.
O Vasus, Rudras, Ādityas, these are your foot-washing [waters];
you follow the ocean standing in the Gandharva, praised on the course of the wind.
Fair one, in your sight may I obtain all seed; in your sight, fair one!

3.10.m:
You are the downward grasps, heard by the gods, bright, bringing brightness!
Satisfy my life;
satisfy my breath;
satisfy my inter-breath;
satisfy my down-breath;
satisfy my eye;
satisfy my ear;
satisfy my speech;
satisfy my self;
satisfy my offspring;
satisfy my houses;
satisfy my cattle;
satisfy my troops!
Satisfied, satisfy me;
pleased, please me;
may they not thirst for me!
At the impulse of the god Savitṛ, with the arms of the Aśvins, with the hands of Pūṣan, I take you.
You are a pressing stone, performing the sacrifice for the gods.
Make this sacrifice aloft with the highest rim;
most well pressed for Indra;
sweet, full of milk;
for Indra, slayer of enemies, [I take] you;
for Indra, bestower of strength, [I take] you;
for Indra, accompanied by the Vasus, [I take] you;
for Indra, accompanied by the Rudras, [I take] you;
for Indra, accompanied by the Ādityas, [I take] you;
for Agni, bestower of the increase of wealth, [I take] you;
for Viṣṇu, you;
for the falcon, bearer of Soma, you;
for Viṣṇu, you!
What light of yours, O Soma, is in heaven,
what on earth, what in the wide intermediate space,
with that make wide space for this lord of sacrifice, for wealth!
Speak above for the sustainer!
You are invigorating, overcoming Vṛtra, approved by generosity, wives of the immortal;
as divine ones, having made this sacrifice among the gods, invited, drink of the Soma!
Do not fear,
do not tremble!
O two firm vessels, be firm;
bestow vigor;
bestow vigor in us!
May I not harm you two;
may you two not harm us!
East, west, north, downward—may those quarters flow to you!
Mother, sound forth;
may you find the enemy!
Thus the third sthānaka called Jyotirika in the Iṭhimikā of the Caraka recension of the glorious Yajurveda in the Kāṭhaka is complete.

4.2.m:
Come, O Vāyu, drinker of the pure [Soma], to us; a thousand are your teams, all-bounteous one!
To you is offered the exhilarating draught, of which, O god, you possess the first drinking!
You are taken with a support;
for Vāyu, you!
O Indra and Vāyu, these [drops] are pressed; come toward them with delights!
For the drops desire you both!
You are taken with a support;
for Vāyu, for Indra and Vāyu, you!
This is your womb;
for the harmonious pair, you!
This Soma is pressed for you two, O Mitra and Varuṇa, who increase truth;
hear this invocation of mine here!
You are taken with a support;
for Mitra and Varuṇa, you!
This is your womb;
for the seekers of truth, you!
Your whip, O Aśvins, sweet and full of pleasantness,
with that sprinkle the sacrifice!
You are taken with a support;
for the Aśvins, you!
This is your womb;
for the sweet pair, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Vāyu, for Indra and Vāyu, you!
This is your womb;
in the wide stride of Viṣṇu!
You are taken with a support;
for Mitra and Varuṇa, you!
This is your womb;
in the wide stride of Viṣṇu!
You are taken with a support;
for the Aśvins, you!
This is your womb;
in the wide stride of Viṣṇu!
Guard that!
May they not harm you!
May the evil-eyed one not gaze down upon you!

4.3.m:
This Vena, born of Pṛśni, drove forth the shining afterbirths in the measure of space;
at the confluence of the waters, of the sun, the inspired poets lick him with songs like a calf.
You are taken with a support;
for Indra, beloved of Śaṇḍa, I take you!
This is your womb;
for heroism, you!
Him in the ancient way, in the former way, in every way, now, the highest state, sitting on the sacrificial grass, winning the sun,
by song you milk the turned-toward enclosure, [singing] which you conquer, [and] among which you grow!
You are taken with a support;
for Sūrya, beloved of Marka, I take you!
This is your womb;
for offspring, you!

4.5.m:
You gods who are eleven in heaven, who are eleven upon earth,
who are eleven dwelling in the waters with majesty, O gods, enjoy this sacrifice!
You are taken with a support, belonging to the Āgrāyaṇa;
enliven the sacrifice; enliven the lord of the sacrifice!
Protect the pressings;
may Viṣṇu protect you;
protect the people with your power!
This is your womb;
for all the gods, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Indra possessed of greatness, possessed of vigor, worthy of praise;
for that great vigor of yours, O Indra, [I take] you;
for Viṣṇu, you!
This is your womb;
for Indra, you!
The head of heaven, the messenger of earth, Vaiśvānara, Agni born in truth,
the sage, the sovereign king, guest of men—let the gods generate him as a vessel in the mouth!
You are taken with a support, belonging to Vaiśvānara;
you are firm, a firm resting place of the firm, the firmest of the unshakeable, the most unshakeable resting place!
This is your womb;
for Vaiśvānara, you!

4.6.m:
You are taken with a support;
for Mitra and Varuṇa, you!
For the recitations I take you, worthy of recitation!
This is your womb;
for Mitra and Varuṇa, you!
You are a renewed oblation;
for the gods, I mix you, pleasing the gods, for the life of the sacrifice!
You are taken with a support;
for Indra, you!
For the recitations I take you, worthy of recitation!
This is your womb;
for Indra, you!
You are a renewed oblation;
for the gods, I mix you, pleasing the gods, for the life of the sacrifice!
You are taken with a support;
for Indra and Agni, you!
For the recitations I take you, worthy of recitation!
This is your womb;
for Indra and Agni, you!
For the gods, I mix you, pleasing the gods, for the life of the sacrifice!
You are taken with a support;
for Indra, you!
For Indra, you!
For the recitations I take you, worthy of recitation!
This is your womb;
for Indra, you!
For the gods, I mix you, pleasing the gods, for the life of the sacrifice!
You are taken with a support;
for Indra and Varuṇa, you!
For the recitations I take you, worthy of recitation!
This is your womb;
for Indra and Varuṇa, you!
You are a renewed oblation;
for the gods, I mix you, pleasing the gods, for the life of the sacrifice!
You are taken with a support;
for Indra and Bṛhaspati, you!
For the recitations I take you, worthy of recitation!
This is your womb;
for Indra and Bṛhaspati, you!
You are a renewed oblation;
for the gods, I mix you, pleasing the gods, for the life of the sacrifice!
You are taken with a support;
for Indra and Viṣṇu, you!
For the recitations I take you, worthy of recitation!
This is your womb;
for Indra and Viṣṇu, you!
You are a renewed oblation;
for the gods, I mix you, pleasing the gods, for the life of the sacrifice!

4.7.m:
You are taken with a support;
for Madhu, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Mādhava, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Śukra, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Śuci, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Nabhas, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Nabhasya, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Iṣa, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Ūrja, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Sahas, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Sahasya, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Tapas, you!
You are taken with a support;
for Tapasya, you!
O Indra and Agni, come to the pressed [Soma], desirable like the misty sky, with our songs,
impelled by our thought, drink of this!
You are taken with a support;
for Indra and Agni, you!
This is your womb;
for Indra and Agni, you!
O protectors, supporters of men, all you gods, come,
generous ones, to the pressed [Soma] of the worshiper!
You are taken with a support;
for all the gods, you!
This is your womb;
for all the gods, you!

4.8.m:
You were born fierce for swift strength, charming, most mighty, of boundless pride;
the Maruts magnified Indra even then, when the mother, most wealthy, bore the hero.
You are taken with a support;
for Indra accompanied by the Maruts!
This is your womb;
for Indra accompanied by the Maruts!
O Indra accompanied by the Maruts, drink Soma here, as you drank of the pressed [juice] at the Śāryāta [sacrifice];
under your guidance, O hero, in your protection, the well-sacrificing poets seek to win [favor].
You are taken with a support;
for Indra accompanied by the Maruts!
This is your womb;
for Indra accompanied by the Maruts!
Indra accompanied by the Maruts, the bull, drink Soma according to your will for battle, for exhilaration;
pour into your belly the wave of sweetness; you are the ancient king of the pressed [juices]!
You are taken with a support;
for Indra accompanied by the Maruts!
This is your womb;
for Indra accompanied by the Maruts!
Indra accompanied by the Maruts, the bull, the growing one, who has no niggardly foe, the heavenly ruler,
all-conquering, fierce, the giver of strength—him we would call here for modern aid!
You are taken with a support;
for Indra accompanied by the Maruts!
This is your womb;
for Indra accompanied by the Maruts!
Great is Indra, who by his might, like Parjanya possessed of rain,
has grown through the praise-songs of Vatsa.
You are taken with a support;
for Great Indra, you!
This is your womb;
for Great Indra, you!
Great is Indra, manly, filling the people, and double-bulwarked, unyielding in strengths;
he has grown toward us for heroic deeds; wide, broad, well-made has he become through the makers.
You are taken with a support;
for Great Indra, you!
This is your womb;
for Great Indra, you!

4.10.m:
Never are you barren, nor, O Indra, do you neglect the worshiper;
ever closer, O generous one, ever more is the gift of the god poured out!
You are taken with a support;
for the Ādityas, you!
Never are you heedless; you watch over both races;
O fourth Āditya, your pressed juice is full of vitality, the immortal [abode] you have assumed in heaven.
You are taken with a support;
for the Ādityas, you!
The sacrifice goes to meet the favor of the gods; O Ādityas, be gracious!
May your good will turn hitherward toward us, which shall find wider room even out of distress!
You are taken with a support;
for the Ādityas, you!
Shine forth, O Āditya, this is your Soma-drink; rejoice in it!
With that which is heavenly rain, I mix you!
With unbeguiled, benevolent guardians, O Savitṛ, guard our household today!
Golden-tongued, for newer welfare, protect [us]; may no speaker of evil have power over us!
You are taken with a support;
for the god Savitṛ, [you]!
You are taken with a support;
you are well-sheltering, well-founded;
homage to the great sprinkler!
This is your womb;
for all the gods, you!

4.11.m:
You are taken with a support.
May I satisfy the cup of you, O drop, pressed by Bṛhaspati, possessing vital power, accompanied by your wife!
O Agni, accompanied by your wife, united with Tvaṣṭṛ, drink the Soma!
You are taken with a support.
You are the bay-colored one, belonging to the yoker of the bay steeds;
mounting the two bays;
for the two bays, you!
Of you, O divine Soma, whose praise-hymn is chanted, whose recitation is recited, whose sacrificial formula is offered,
may I satisfy the cup belonging to the one who has the bay steeds!
You two are the bays; you are the parched grains belonging to the one who has the bay steeds, with the Soma of Indra.
O Agni, you purify our life-spans; spur forth strength and nourishment for us;
drive misfortune far away!
You are taken with a support;
for Agni, endowed with splendor, [I take] you!
This is your womb;
for Agni, endowed with splendor!
That strength of his flared up, when Indra rolled together both
heaven and earth like a hide.
You are taken with a support;
for Indra, endowed with vigor, [I take] you!
This is your womb;
for Indra, endowed with vigor!
His banners have appeared, his rays across the peoples,
shining like fires.
You are taken with a support;
for the Sun, endowed with brilliance, [I take] you!
This is your womb;
for the Sun, endowed with brilliance!
The two bay steeds bear Indra of irresistible power,
to the praises of the ṛṣis and to the sacrifice of mortals.
You are taken with a support;
for Indra, possessor of the bay steeds, [I take] you!
This is your womb;
for Indra, possessor of the bay steeds!

4.13.m:
For King Varuṇa made a broad path for the Sun to follow;
he made feet to step where there is no foot; and he turns away whatever pierces the heart.
A hundred are your physicians, O king, a thousand; may your good will be broad and deep;
drive Nirṛti far away; loosen from us whatever sin has been committed!
The face of Agni entered the waters, the Son of Waters protecting the divine power.
In house after house you will worship the kindling stick, O Agni; toward you the tongue of ghee shall rise up.
Your heart is in the ocean, within the waters; may the plants and waters enter into you;
we would worship you, of the sacrifice, O lord of the sacrifice, with the hymn of praise, with the words of homage, svāhā!
O Avabhṛtha [bath], O Nicuṅkuṇa, you are gliding softly, O Nicuṅkuṇa;
wash away from us the sin committed against the gods, by the gods;
wash away [the sin] committed against mortals, by mortals;
protect us, O god, from broad harm!
O divine waters, this is your embryo;
well-pleased, well-carried, I have carried it for you;
among the gods speak of us as well-doers!
Stepped upon is the fetter of Varuṇa!
Struck away is the fetter of Varuṇa!
Of you, cleansed in the waters, O divine Soma, praised by men, whatever portion is winning cattle, winning horses—invited, I take the portion of that invited [Soma].
Thrown back is the fetter of Varuṇa!
Homage to the fetter of Varuṇa!
Step up, bringing offspring, life-span, and brilliance; then may we be fragrant in our houses;
may the meters join with the Gāyatrī; may wealth and sacrifice adhere to us!
Well-pleased, the child has entered the waters.
O Unnetṛ, lead us up to better [fortune]!
You are kindling wood: may we thrive!
You are a fuel stick: may we kindle well!
You are splendor: place splendor in me!
I have now walked along the waters; we have united with their sap;
rich in milk have I come, O Agni; unite me with brilliance!
Unite me, O Agni, with brilliance, and with offspring, and with wealth;
may the gods know of me, may Indra know together with the ṛṣis!

5.6.m:
The sacrifice has gone to the people of the gods;
thence may the blessing of the sacrifice come to me!
The sacrifice has gone to the Fathers, the serpents, the Gandharvas, the waters, the plants, the five peoples, to people;
thence may the blessing of the sacrifice come to me!
I grasp you for the support of the five winds;
I grasp you for the support of the five waters;
I grasp you for the support of the five backs;
I grasp you for the support of the five quarters;
I grasp you for the support of the five tribes!
The earth is ours;
the oblation is the gods';
the blessings belong to the sacrificer.
I grasp you for the support of the five-apertured caru!
You are the dear domain of the gods,
the unassailable place of sacrifice.
With the deities I grasp you for the deities!
Those gods, slayers of the sacrifice, thieves of the sacrifice, who sit upon the earth — / may Agni protect me from them; may we go to the righteous!
Those nights of yours, O Savitṛ, that lead to the gods, which have embraced the thousandfold sacrifice — / together with all houses and with offspring now at first, mounting heaven, cross through the dark realms!
Those gods, slayers of the sacrifice, thieves of the sacrifice, who sit in the intermediate space — / may Vāyu protect me from them; may we go to the righteous!
We have come, O Mitra and Varuṇa, to the choice portion of nights which is yours, / seizing the vault in the world of the righteous on the third back above the light of heaven!
Those gods, slayers of the sacrifice, thieves of the sacrifice, who sit in heaven — / may Sūrya protect me from them; may we go to the righteous!
Wherewith they brought together milk for Indra with the highest oblation, O Jātavedas, / therewith, O Agni, do you also make him thrive; place him in the preeminence among those of noble birth!
Possessing cows, O Agni, possessing sheep, possessing horses is the sacrifice, accompanied by men, an unforgettable companion; / rich in refreshing drink is it, O Asura, rich in offspring, long-lasting wealth, broad-bottomed, full of council-gatherings!
O Agni, protector of vows, I have kept the vow;
I have been able to do it;
we declare that to you;
protect that for us!
Thus is the fifth sthānaka complete, called Yajamāna, in the Iṭhimikā of the Caraka school in the glorious Yajurveda of the Kaṭhas.

6.8.m:
The cooking of the rice mess, the Gārhapatya, the Āhavanīya, the midst of the gaming ground, the calling place—
this, truly, is the five-footed Virāj.
That very [Virāj] he attains;
that he secures.
For he who has secured it becomes the best among men.
If the time of the evening Agnihotra should pass by, he should offer, [saying:] 'At dusk of the morning, svāhā!'
That very [utterance] is the oblation there;
thereby it is not missed by him.
If the time of the morning Agnihotra should pass by, he should offer, [saying:] 'At day of the morning, svāhā!'
That very [utterance] is the oblation there;
thereby it is not missed by him.
He should not utter 'svāhā';
the utterance 'svāhā' separates the oblation of the Agnihotra.
When speech resounds, then he should offer;
for that is the vaṣaṭ-call of the Agnihotra.
[Saying:] 'Agni, united with day, with earth'—
Heaven and Earth, Agni—these indeed he pleases;
these he secures.
[Saying:] 'United with the god Savitṛ'—
for without Savitṛ there is no oblation.
[Saying:] 'United with Pūṣan, with the intermediate space'—
cattle, truly, are Pūṣan; cattle are the intermediate space;
cattle indeed he secures.
[Saying:] 'United with the night possessing Indra, svāhā!'—
over the night indeed he offers it;
for without Indra there is no oblation.
The gods, truly, offered the Agnihotra in the morning;
therefore the Bṛhat, the great, was born in the morning.
[Saying:] 'United with the day possessing Indra, svāhā!'—
connected with the Bṛhat, truly, is the day; connected with the Bṛhat is Sūrya;
both the day and Sūrya are conquered for him and offered upon.
Belonging to the Anuṣṭubh, truly, is the night; belonging to the Triṣṭubh is the day;
upon both the night and the day he thus offers.
With: 'O unassailable Agni, enjoy, svāhā!' he offers the second oblation;
just as one cuts off [portions] for Agni, just so is that.
With: 'You have pleased your own body, O Agni; you have sacrificed to Heaven and Earth; place vigor in us,' having anointed a blade of grass, he throws it [into the fire];
that is the completion, the setting at ease.
What is unappeased of the Agnihotra injures creatures;
when, having anointed a blade of grass, he throws it in,
thereby indeed he appeases it.
With: 'Agni, lord of the house, enjoy, svāhā!' he offers in the Gārhapatya with the dipping spoon;
just as one performs the wife's sacrifices, just so is that.
He, truly, reflects upon this,
that having placed [the pot] on the fire in the west, he offers in the east.
When he offers in the Gārhapatya with the dipping spoon,
thereby indeed he pleases him;
he makes him not brood.
In his progeny an Agnihotra-cow is born, day by day he becomes better off, whose Agnihotra is offered thus.
